# Scratch run logs.
#
# The debugging workflow here is `node verify.mjs > out.txt` and then reading the
# file, because the suite prints ~830 lines and terminal output gets truncated.
# Sixteen of these had accumulated in the root and been committed before anyone
# noticed. None of them belong in the history.
*.txt
*.log

# node_modules is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is committed so a clone runs offline with nothing to install, which is the
# whole reason three.js is served from disk rather than a CDN. Adding it here
# would not untrack what is already tracked, but it would silently drop any file
# added by a future `npm install`. See the README.

# Wrangler's local state: the miniflare cache, the local Durable Object storage
# and its temp bundles. Recreated on every `npm run dev:mp` and machine-specific.
# Also listed in .assetsignore, for a different reason — see that file.
.wrangler/

# Miniflare drops a second cache HERE, inside node_modules, which matters because
# node_modules is deliberately committed (see the note above and the README). Without
# this line, running `npm run dev:mp` once puts a machine-specific cache into the
# repository along with the vendored dependency it is meant to be sitting beside.
node_modules/.mf/

# OS and editor cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
